You don't need rstudio to knit, you can just run an R script that calls `knit("myfile.Rmd")` or what not.  Of course you can also run rstudio in the cloud (e.g. on an amazon web server, though you might ask the maintainers of your university HPC if they would consider supporting rstudio server installation.)

On Thu, Mar 6, 2014 at 2:46 PM, Jeff Newmiller <jdne...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> One solution is to separate the computation from the presentation. Put your computations in an R file, run them at the computing facility of your choice to generate result objects in memory, and save.image to store them. Move the RData file to your workstation and just load the RData file in your Rmd/Rnw file and generate presentable results.
